## Summary

When a Messages (`/v1/messages`) stream with `tools` is relayed via passthrough and the upstream flushes SSE lines across separate `Read` chunks (e.g. `event: content_block_start\n` in one read and `data: {...}\n` in the next), `anthropicTextCalls.write` splits `t.buf[:i+1]` with `bytes.SplitAfter(..., []byte("\n"))`.

Because `t.buf[:i+1]` ends with `\n`, `bytes.SplitAfter` always appends a trailing empty slice `""`. `anthropicTextCalls.line` checks `len(bytes.TrimSpace(line)) > 0` and mistakes that trailing `""` for the blank line that terminates an SSE event, calling `t.event` prematurely at the end of every `Read`:

1. **Empty-data `content_block_start` crash (`Unexpected end of JSON input`)**: When `event: content_block_start\n` arrives in read 1, the trailing `""` flushes `t.event(ev)` immediately; because there is no `data:` line yet, `t.event` forwards `event: content_block_start\n` downstream. When `data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":0,"content_block":{"type":"text","text":""}}\n` arrives in read 2, the trailing `""` flushes `t.event` again, which withholds the empty text block start in `t.startHeld` and returns nothing. When the real blank line `\n` arrives in read 3, it passes through, leaving downstream with `event: content_block_start\n\n` (no `data:` line).
2. **Concatenated JSON payloads (`Unexpected non-whitespace character after JSON`)**: When `event: content_block_start\n` and `data: {...}\n` arrive in read 1 without the trailing blank line `\n`, the synthetic `""` flushes `t.event` and stores `t.startHeld` with only a single trailing `\n`. When `t.startHeld` is later prepended to the first `content_block_delta`, the two events lack a blank-line separator and their `data:` lines are joined into one event.

## What changed

- `internal/gateway/textcalls_anthropic.go`:
  - Replace the line-by-line `bytes.SplitAfter` + `t.line` accumulator with `tidyEvents(t.buf, t.event)` and `eventData(ev)` (matching `responsesTextCalls`, `phaseTidy`, and `idTidy`), so `t.event` only runs once a complete SSE event boundary (`eventEnd`) has been buffered.
  - Copy `ev` into `t.startHeld` and `t.stopHeld` (`append([]byte(nil), ev...)`) before `tidyEvents` reuses the underlying buffer slice.

## Branch & Patch

- Fork branch: [`oDaiSuno:fix/anthropic-textcalls-split-sse`](https://github.com/oDaiSuno/magpie/tree/fix/anthropic-textcalls-split-sse) (head `c88b171f72df33e133ca4791bd1e59ab2be2b8f5`)

